# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Runtime artifacts (normally live outside the repo, but ignore just in case)
*.log
.cache/
chromium-profile/

# Live slide content and uploaded images - edited on disk through the slide
# editor (src/editor.py), not through git. Excluded so autoupdate.sh's
# rollback (`git reset --hard`) can never discard someone's slide edits
# along with reverting broken code; it only ever touches tracked code.
# install.sh seeds these from web/slides.example.json and
# web/assets/src-logo.example.png (both still tracked) on a fresh install,
# exactly once, same pattern as config.example.env -> config.env.
web/slides.json
web/assets/*
!web/assets/*.example.png
